.TH MODMAN.CONF 5 "2026-04-22" "modman" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
modman.conf \- runtime configuration for modman and modman-gui
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/modman.conf
.br
.B ~/.config/modman/modman.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmodman.conf\fR stores simple key-value settings for the modman backend.
The parser is intentionally strict and does not execute shell code.
.SH FORMAT
Each non-empty non-comment line must use the form:
.br
.B KEY=VALUE
.P
Supported scalar values may be unquoted, single-quoted, or double-quoted.
Whitespace around the key and value is trimmed.
.P
Unsafe shell substitution syntax is rejected, including:
.IP \(bu 2
\fB$(...)\fR
.IP \(bu 2
backticks
.IP \(bu 2
\fB${...}\fR
.SH SEARCH ORDER
.IP "1." 4
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/modman/modman.conf\fR
.IP "2." 4
\fB~/.config/modman/modman.conf\fR
.IP "3." 4
\fB/etc/modman.conf\fR
.IP "4." 4
\fB/usr/share/modman/modman.conf\fR
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B MODMAN_BIN
Path to the modman executable.
.TP
.B DOWNLOAD_DIR
Directory for downloaded modules.
.TP
.B AUFS_INITRD_PREFIX
Prefix used to detect initrd-loaded modules. For mkinitcpio-rootaufs2 set to
.IR /run/archroot/live/memory/images .
.TP
.B MODMAN_IGNORE_DEPS
Whitespace-separated glob patterns of dependency names that
.B modman -S
must skip during dependency resolution. Use when deps are bundled into a
distribution base module (e.g. \fI030-*\fR groups baked into \fI001-zz\fR).
Default: empty (no deps skipped).
.TP
.B EXT
File extension for module containers (without leading dot). Used by
.B modman
to glob the local cache, strip suffixes from package names, and detect
bundle files in aufs branches. Override when using an alternate container
format. Default: \fIpfs\fR.
.TP
.B AUFS_SYSTEM_PATH
Prefix used for mounted module paths.
.TP
.B CMD_LOAD
Optional command override for loading modules.
.TP
.B CMD_UNLOAD
Optional command override for unloading modules.
.TP
.B IFS_SEP
Optional field separator value for machine-readable output.
.TP
.B LAYERING_OVERRIDE
Optional override for runtime layering detection.
.TP
.B PFSLOAD_ALLOW_LOWER
Right-click menu command for loading a module to the lower AUFS layer.
String value holds the full command (e.g. \fIpfsload -l\fR).
Empty or absent \(-> menu item is hidden.
.TP
.B PFSLOAD_ALLOW_TORAM
Right-click menu command for loading a module to RAM (e.g. \fIpfsload -r\fR).
.TP
.B PFSLOAD_ALLOW_LOWER_TORAM
Right-click menu command for lower layer + RAM (e.g. \fIpfsload -l -r\fR).
.TP
.B PFSLOAD_ALLOW_UPPER_TORAM
Right-click menu command for upper layer + RAM (e.g. \fIpfsload -u -r\fR).
.SS Update check on login
.PP
The following keys control the behaviour of \fBmodman-update-check\fR(8),
a helper script launched at login via XDG autostart.
.PP
.B Important:
\fBmodman-update-check\fR \fBdoes not apply updates automatically\fR.
It only checks for available updates and notifies the user via
\fInotify-send\fR. To apply updates use \fBmodman --update\fR
or \fBmodman --update-all\fR manually.
.TP
.B UPDATE_CHECK_ON_LOGIN
Enable update checking at login.
.RS
.TP
.B 1
Enabled (default). \fBmodman-update-check\fR is launched automatically
via \fI/etc/xdg/autostart/modman-update-check.desktop\fR at session start.
.TP
.B 0
Disabled. The script exits immediately without calling \fBmodman\fR.
.RE
.TP
.B UPDATE_CHECK_OPEN_GUI
Open \fBmodman-gui --updates\fR when updates are found.
.RS
.TP
.B 0
Notification via \fInotify-send\fR only (default).
.TP
.B 1
Additionally open the GUI with the updates tab in the background.
.RE
.TP
.B UPDATE_BLACKLIST_FILE
Path to the update blacklist file. Format: TSV, one entry per line:
.RS
.PP
.B identity\etversion
.PP
Each entry blocks a specific version of a specific module. Matching is
exact \(em glob patterns are not supported.
.PP
Default: \fI${MODMAN_STATE_DIR}/update-blacklist.tsv\fR
(typically \fI/var/lib/modman/update-blacklist.tsv\fR). If the default path is
used and the old \fI${CACHE_DIR}/update-blacklist.tsv\fR exists, \fBmodman\fR
copies it to the persistent state path on the next blacklist operation.
.PP
The file's directory is created automatically on the first entry added via
\fBmodman --update-blacklist-add\fR. For manual management the file can be
edited directly \(em each line must contain exactly two TAB-separated fields.
.RE
.SS Reboot behaviour
.PP
When an updated module contains changes that require a reboot
(\fBreboot_required=1\fR in machine output), \fBmodman\fR:
.IP \(bu 2
Emits the literal string \fB\[u043D]\[u0443]\[u0436]\[u043D]\[u0430] \[u043F]\[u0435]\[u0440]\[u0435]\[u0437]\[u0430]\[u0433]\[u0440]\[u0443]\[u0437]\[u043A]\[u0430]\fR in machine output after the \fBapplied\fR line.
This Russian literal (\(lqreboot required\(rq) is part of the machine contract;
parsers must match it verbatim.
.IP \(bu 2
Displays a warning in the GUI.
.IP \(bu 2
Writes a note to \fIupdate.log\fR alongside the updated file.
.PP
A reboot is never performed automatically. The user must reboot manually.
.SH SECURITY
The configuration loader never invokes a shell, does not support \fBsource\fR,
and ignores unsupported shell constructs outside the documented key-value format.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR modman (8)
